WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.907
Communication Principles.

2
00:00:02.187 --> 00:00:06.539
Day 16 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the Communication phase.

3
00:00:08.289 --> 00:00:09.313
The key idea.

4
00:00:09.593 --> 00:00:11.727
Communication is not what you say.

5
00:00:12.007 --> 00:00:13.991
It's what the other person understands.

6
00:00:14.271 --> 00:00:17.343
Seven rules, then frameworks you can reuse anywhere.

7
00:00:18.693 --> 00:00:19.546
Part 1.

8
00:00:19.826 --> 00:00:21.234
The communication stack.

9
00:00:22.484 --> 00:00:24.553
Each layer depends on the one under it.

10
00:00:24.833 --> 00:00:26.561
Hover a layer to bring it forward.

11
00:00:27.911 --> 00:00:28.850
Step 6:

12
00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:33.055
Trust: built when layers 1 to 5 stay consistent over time.

13
00:00:33.335 --> 00:00:34.295
Step 5:

14
00:00:34.575 --> 00:00:37.967
Confidence: steady voice, no over-apology, ownership.

15
00:00:38.247 --> 00:00:39.207
Step 4:

16
00:00:39.487 --> 00:00:42.197
Tone: polite, firm, warm, matched to the moment.

17
00:00:42.477 --> 00:00:43.394
Step 3:

18
00:00:43.674 --> 00:00:46.618
Structure: point first, then reasons, then the ask.

19
00:00:46.898 --> 00:00:47.815
Step 2:

20
00:00:48.095 --> 00:00:51.039
Clarity: simple words, one idea per sentence.

21
00:00:51.319 --> 00:00:52.237
Step 1:

22
00:00:52.517 --> 00:00:55.418
Listening: understand before you try to be understood.

23
00:00:56.768 --> 00:00:57.643
Part 2.

24
00:00:57.923 --> 00:00:59.075
The 7 rules.

25
00:01:00.325 --> 00:01:01.797
Lead with the point (BLUF:

26
00:01:02.077 --> 00:01:03.527
Bottom Line Up Front).

27
00:01:03.807 --> 00:01:06.133
Developers often tell the story in order:

28
00:01:06.413 --> 00:01:09.165
So I was looking at the logs, and then I noticed....

29
00:01:09.445 --> 00:01:13.071
Busy listeners stop paying attention before the point arrives.

30
00:01:14.421 --> 00:01:15.787
Here is a quick table:

31
00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:17.944
Story first, and Point first.

32
00:01:18.224 --> 00:01:23.408
So yesterday I was debugging and I found the cache wasn't... and then I checked the config and...:

33
00:01:23.688 --> 00:01:25.693
The release is blocked by a cache bug.

34
00:01:25.973 --> 00:01:27.296
I need 1 more day.

35
00:01:27.576 --> 00:01:28.771
Here's what happened...

36
00:01:30.121 --> 00:01:32.339
Know your audience: the altitude rule.

37
00:01:32.619 --> 00:01:35.670
Pitch the same issue at a different height for each listener:

38
00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:38.385
Here is a quick table:

39
00:01:38.665 --> 00:01:40.927
Audience, and Cares about, and Talk about.

40
00:01:41.207 --> 00:01:42.487
CEO or Exec.

41
00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:43.748
Cares about:

42
00:01:44.028 --> 00:01:46.588
Revenue, customers, risk, reputation.

43
00:01:46.868 --> 00:01:47.785
Talk about:

44
00:01:48.065 --> 00:01:50.241
Impact, decision needed, timeline.

45
00:01:50.521 --> 00:01:51.417
Manager.

46
00:01:51.697 --> 00:01:52.679
Cares about:

47
00:01:52.959 --> 00:01:55.092
Delivery, team health, surprises.

48
00:01:55.372 --> 00:01:56.289
Talk about:

49
00:01:56.569 --> 00:01:58.809
Status, risks, options, what you need.

50
00:01:59.089 --> 00:02:00.156
Peer engineer.

51
00:02:00.436 --> 00:02:01.417
Cares about:

52
00:02:01.697 --> 00:02:03.148
How it works, trade-offs.

53
00:02:03.428 --> 00:02:04.345
Talk about:

54
00:02:04.625 --> 00:02:06.012
Design, code, data.

55
00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:07.060
Junior.

56
00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:08.321
Cares about:

57
00:02:08.601 --> 00:02:10.948
Learning, doing it right, not looking silly.

58
00:02:11.228 --> 00:02:12.145
Talk about:

59
00:02:12.425 --> 00:02:14.452
Steps, reasons, encouragement.

60
00:02:14.732 --> 00:02:16.225
Customer or stranger.

61
00:02:16.505 --> 00:02:17.487
Cares about:

62
00:02:17.767 --> 00:02:19.089
Their problem solved.

63
00:02:19.369 --> 00:02:20.287
Talk about:

64
00:02:20.567 --> 00:02:22.188
Plain language, next step.

65
00:02:23.538 --> 00:02:24.989
One idea per sentence.

66
00:02:25.269 --> 00:02:27.274
Short sentences sound confident.

67
00:02:27.554 --> 00:02:30.903
Long sentences sound like you're still working out what you think.

68
00:02:32.253 --> 00:02:33.661
Specific beats vague.

69
00:02:33.941 --> 00:02:34.709
Vague:

70
00:02:34.989 --> 00:02:43.587
It's kind of slow. then Specific: p95 latency went from 200 ms to 1.4 s after Tuesday's deploy.

71
00:02:43.867 --> 00:02:44.635
Vague:

72
00:02:44.915 --> 00:02:46.387
Soon. then Specific:

73
00:02:46.667 --> 00:02:48.267
By Thursday 5 pm.

74
00:02:49.617 --> 00:02:51.963
Always end with an ask or a next step.

75
00:02:52.243 --> 00:03:01.566
Every message should answer what do you want from me? ...so can you approve the extra day?...I'll update you at 4 pm....no action needed, FYI only.

76
00:03:02.916 --> 00:03:04.239
Polite is not weak.

77
00:03:04.519 --> 00:03:05.777
Firm is not rude.

78
00:03:06.057 --> 00:03:07.423
Here is a quick table:

79
00:03:07.703 --> 00:03:09.857
Too weak, and Balanced, and Too harsh.

80
00:03:10.137 --> 00:03:12.185
Sorry, I might be wrong, but maybe...

81
00:03:12.465 --> 00:03:13.319
Balanced:

82
00:03:13.599 --> 00:03:14.879
I see it differently.

83
00:03:15.159 --> 00:03:16.097
Here's why.

84
00:03:16.377 --> 00:03:17.295
Too harsh:

85
00:03:17.575 --> 00:03:18.513
That's wrong.

86
00:03:18.793 --> 00:03:20.713
If it's okay, could I possibly...

87
00:03:20.993 --> 00:03:21.847
Balanced:

88
00:03:22.127 --> 00:03:23.791
Could I take 10 minutes on this?

89
00:03:24.071 --> 00:03:24.988
Too harsh:

90
00:03:25.268 --> 00:03:26.399
I need this now.

91
00:03:27.749 --> 00:03:29.135
Confirm understanding.

92
00:03:29.415 --> 00:03:32.018
Close important conversations with a recap:

93
00:03:32.298 --> 00:03:33.471
Just to confirm:

94
00:03:33.751 --> 00:03:37.015
I'll fix the cache by Thursday, and you'll tell the product team.

95
00:03:37.295 --> 00:03:38.042
Right?

96
00:03:39.392 --> 00:03:40.288
Part 3.

97
00:03:40.568 --> 00:03:42.040
Reusable frameworks.

98
00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:44.655
PREP (give an opinion).

99
00:03:44.935 --> 00:03:47.858
Point, then Reason, then Example, then Point again.

100
00:03:48.138 --> 00:03:50.549
I recommend Postgres over Mongo (P).

101
00:03:50.829 --> 00:03:54.434
Our data is relational: orders, items, payments (R).

102
00:03:54.714 --> 00:03:59.386
Last year's reporting rewrite took 3 months because of joins in Mongo (E).

103
00:03:59.666 --> 00:04:01.970
So Postgres is the safer choice (P).

104
00:04:03.320 --> 00:04:04.877
SBAR (report an issue).

105
00:04:05.157 --> 00:04:09.040
Situation, then Background, then Assessment, then Recommendation.

106
00:04:09.320 --> 00:04:12.285
Checkout is failing for 8% of users (S).

107
00:04:12.565 --> 00:04:16.277
It started after the 2 pm payment-SDK upgrade (B).

108
00:04:16.557 --> 00:04:19.437
I think the new SDK times out under load (A).

109
00:04:19.717 --> 00:04:23.280
I recommend we roll back now and investigate tomorrow (R).

110
00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:26.635
STAR (tell a story or interview).

111
00:04:26.915 --> 00:04:29.881
Situation, then Task, then Action, then Result.

112
00:04:30.161 --> 00:04:32.123
Our deploys took 2 hours (S).

113
00:04:32.403 --> 00:04:34.238
I was asked to cut that down (T).

114
00:04:34.518 --> 00:04:37.825
I parallelised the test suite and added caching (A).

115
00:04:38.105 --> 00:04:40.366
Deploys now take 18 minutes (R).

116
00:04:41.716 --> 00:04:43.721
What or So what or Now what (status).

117
00:04:44.001 --> 00:04:44.556
What:

118
00:04:44.836 --> 00:04:47.524
API migration is 70% done.

119
00:04:47.804 --> 00:04:48.636
So what:

120
00:04:48.916 --> 00:04:51.348
We're on track, but the auth piece is risky.

121
00:04:51.628 --> 00:04:52.481
Now what:

122
00:04:52.761 --> 00:04:55.961
I'll pair with Priya on auth tomorrow; update on Friday.

123
00:04:57.311 --> 00:04:58.229
Part 4.

124
00:04:58.509 --> 00:05:00.407
Words to cut and words to use.

125
00:05:01.657 --> 00:05:03.023
Here is a quick table:

126
00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:07.719
Cut (filler or weak), and Use instead. basically, actually, like, you know:

127
00:05:07.999 --> 00:05:09.663
(silence, a short pause).

128
00:05:09.943 --> 00:05:11.351
I think maybe we could...:

129
00:05:11.631 --> 00:05:14.447
I suggest we... / My recommendation is...

130
00:05:14.727 --> 00:05:15.985
Sorry to bother you:

131
00:05:16.265 --> 00:05:17.844
Do you have 5 minutes for...?

132
00:05:18.124 --> 00:05:19.361
Does that make sense?:

133
00:05:19.641 --> 00:05:21.113
What questions do you have?

134
00:05:21.393 --> 00:05:22.268
I'll try:

135
00:05:22.548 --> 00:05:25.065
I will / I can't commit to that, but I can...

136
00:05:25.345 --> 00:05:26.519
It's not my fault:

137
00:05:26.799 --> 00:05:29.231
Here's what happened and what I'm doing about it.

138
00:05:29.511 --> 00:05:31.217
No problem (after thanks):

139
00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:32.500
Happy to help.

140
00:05:33.850 --> 00:05:34.810
Part 5.

141
00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:36.477
Practice conversation:

142
00:05:36.757 --> 00:05:38.527
Point first, with your manager.

143
00:05:39.777 --> 00:05:41.804
Here is how the conversation goes.

144
00:05:42.084 --> 00:05:44.175
How's the payment integration going?

145
00:05:44.455 --> 00:05:45.969
It'll be one day late:

146
00:05:46.249 --> 00:05:48.084
Thursday instead of Wednesday.

147
00:05:48.364 --> 00:05:51.628
The bank's sandbox was down for six hours yesterday.

148
00:05:51.908 --> 00:05:53.017
Okay.

149
00:05:53.297 --> 00:05:54.919
Is anything else at risk?

150
00:05:55.199 --> 00:05:55.903
No.

151
00:05:56.183 --> 00:05:58.956
The rest is on track, and the tests are done.

152
00:05:59.236 --> 00:06:00.772
Do you need anything from me?

153
00:06:02.122 --> 00:06:03.722
The conversation continues.

154
00:06:04.002 --> 00:06:06.818
Yes, could you ask the bank for a backup sandbox?

155
00:06:07.098 --> 00:06:08.613
Then it won't happen again.

156
00:06:08.893 --> 00:06:10.642
Sure, I'll email them today.

157
00:06:11.992 --> 00:06:13.528
That's the end of this lesson.

158
00:06:13.808 --> 00:06:18.480
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

159
00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:24.861
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

